course: dictionary
lesson: 13144
title: One word, two places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A foreman is a noun for a person in charge of a group of workers. The plural is foremen. Look at the clues around the word to see who the foreman is and what they do. «The foreman of the building site told the builders where to lay the bricks.» The words told and where tell you the foreman gives the orders.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another place. «The jury foreman stood up and read out the verdict.» A jury is a group of people who listen to a court case. The foreman speaks for them. The word is the same, but the clues (jury, verdict) show that this is a court, not a factory.
explain: Many people now use gender-neutral words, such as supervisor or foreperson, which can be used for anyone. Foreman is still common, and you will see it in older books and in many workplaces.
fact: Foreman is a noun. Its plural is foremen.
fact: «Foreman» means a worker in charge of a group of workers, for example on a building site or in a factory.
fact: In a court, «foreman» means the person who speaks for the jury.
fact: Other words for a person in charge of workers include supervisor, forewoman and foreperson.
exercise: «The foreman of the building site checked that the wall was straight.» Who is the foreman? | A builder who is new to the job | A visitor who came to look at the view | A bricklayer's tool | *The person in charge of the builders
exercise: «The jury foreman read out the verdict in the courtroom.» What does foreman mean here? | The lawyer who asks questions | *The person who speaks for the jury | A person who is on trial | The judge who wears a wig
exercise: Which word means about the same as foreman in a factory? | Customer | Plumber | *Supervisor | Student
test: In «The foreman told the workers to stop for lunch», who gives the orders? | The lunch cook | Workers | A visitor | *The foreman
test: What is the plural of foreman? | *Foremen | Foremans | Foreman | Foremens
exam: Based on the word jury in «The jury foreman stood up», where would you find a foreman like this? | In a school playground | *In a court | On a farm | At a seaside cafe
